# Aider repo-map / context noise filter for TGW (Dave, 2026-07-15).
# .gitignore already excludes these paths from the repo; this is defense-in-depth
# so Aider's repo map and /add never pull them in even under --add-gitignore-files.
# Source research: docs/TGW-Plan-Vault/inbox/tigwa/Deepseek-v4-flash-aider-config-tweaks.txt
#
# Now tracked in git (todo #1424, see .gitignore's !.aiderignore note) so that
# every fresh `git worktree add` (aider_run_task's task_slug isolation path)
# actually gets this file, not just whichever checkout someone hand-edited it in.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Flutter/Dart (apps/tgw_app is the live app; flutter/ is the vendored 2.3GB SDK clone)
apps/tgw_app/build/
apps/tgw_app/.dart_tool/
flutter/
*.g.dart
*.freezed.dart

# Git / editor / secrets
.git/
.aider*
!.aider.conf.yml
!.aiderignore
.env
.env.*
secrets/

# Large / generated data, not source
tgwcatalog.json
tgwcatalog.csv
catalog.migrated.json*
*.log

# Repo-root symlinks into /home/db/tgw-flake/ (todo #1365) -- tgw has no read
# access into /home/db, and `nix` resolves to a directory. Aider's --yes
# mention-auto-add treats git-tracked symlinks exactly like regular tracked
# files (GitRepo.get_tracked_files() adds any blob-type tree entry, and git
# stores symlinks as blobs), so any reply that mentions the word "nix" while
# discussing this exact problem gets it auto-added, the read fails
# (IsADirectoryError / PermissionError), the edit can't apply, and the retry
# loop burns the hardcoded 3-reflection cap without ever landing a fix
# (todo #1424, reproduced 3x on todo #1365). GitRepo.ignored_file() already
# consults this file before returning "addable" files, so this is a complete
# fix at the config layer -- no code change to aider_mcp_server.py needed.
/nix
/flake.nix
/flake.lock
